{"entryId":"1580","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1580:1","sourceSha256":"9e9c485e4a05d412c386deaea9f7c2b1c393d868780f31811fe6d11206dfd3e0","englishSha256":"c83144c9936f2f34ea09a2b0ac0b32db5af3d6e0532f4aa615d30d2a46cc63fb","citations":[{"id":"1580:1:citation-01","he":[0,34],"en":[30,45],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_54b.7"},"reference":"Bava Metzia 54b:7","assessment":"The exact Abaye formula in Bava Metzia is 54b:7 in the checked witness. Retain original 44b in an annotation and compare the two distinct Talmudic passages.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Metzia 54b:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_54b.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1580:1:citation-02","he":[35,50],"en":[47,60],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_14b.12"},"reference":"Kiddushin 14b:12","assessment":"The direct Kiddushin unit explicitly narrates Tavyomi transmitting a ruling in Abaye’s name.","evidence":[{"reference":"Kiddushin 14b:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_14b.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1580:1:citation-03","he":[52,77],"en":[78,92],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_41b.15"},"reference":"Bava Kamma 41b:15","assessment":"The cited Bava Kamma names Tavyomi in Rava’s name. The difference is specifically about which word was said first.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Kamma 41b:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_41b.15"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1580:1:citation-04","he":[118,143],"en":[173,211],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_72b.2"},"reference":"Kiddushin 72b:2","assessment":"Kiddushin preserves this succession motif in the checked edition. Heilprin’s resulting biographical inference and alternative of mediated transmission remain attributed.","evidence":[{"reference":"Kiddushin 72b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_72b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1580:1:citation-05","he":[168,219],"en":[307,347],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Berakhot_2.1.8"},"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Berakhot 2:1:8","assessment":"The Yerushalmi directly names Rabbi Tavyomi asking Rabbi Chizkiyah about attention in the first verse. The transmitted title is Rabbi rather than Rav in this witness. The Chizkiyah/Abaye report is a different claim.","evidence":[{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Berakhot 2:1:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Berakhot_2.1.8"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"}]},{"id":"1580:1:citation-06","he":[221,241],"en":[353,375],"target":{"entry":1223,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 1223:1","assessment":"The internal locator is the Chizkiyah article, which explicitly cites Bavli transmission in Abaye’s name and separately lists the Tavyomi question. The Bavli uses Chizkiyah or Rav Chizkiyah depending on passage. Neither comparison proves one historical identity across the two corpora.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1223:1","target":{"entry":1223,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1223:3","target":{"entry":1223,"paragraph":3},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Chullin 111b:18","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_111b.18"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 38b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_38b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 108b:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_108b.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4,5],"holds":[{"raw":"וביום שמת רבא נולד רב אשי","reason":"The witness speaks of Rav Ashi in the birth succession motif; this and the chronology inference depend on the literary notice and do not establish whether any named transmitter heard a statement directly.","evidence":[{"reference":"Kiddushin 72b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_72b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"Corrected the Bava Metzia locator with the received 44b in the revision record. The Chizkiyah article corroborates that this is an internal reference. Preserve chronology as a source argument and both ways of hearing a teaching in someone’s name.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Bava Metzia 54b:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_54b.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Kiddushin 14b:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_14b.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Kamma 41b:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_41b.15"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Kiddushin 72b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_72b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Berakhot 2:1:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Berakhot_2.1.8"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1223:1","target":{"entry":1223,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1223:3","target":{"entry":1223,"paragraph":3},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Chullin 111b:18","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_111b.18"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 38b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_38b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"r